WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.768 --> 00:00:04.637 align:start size:78% position:22% line:0%
- Hello, I'm Gav.
- I'm Dan.

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:08.174 align:start position:0% line:0%
And welcome to the final episode
of "Planet Slow Mo."

00:00:08.207 --> 00:00:11.277
I feel like it'd be a crime
if we didn't go out with a bang.

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:12.745
Well, how about multi-colored
bangs?

00:00:12.778 --> 00:00:15.148
- I like it.
- Yeah. Strong.

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:23.222 align:start size:56% position:44%
Today, we're
in Bastrop, Texas.

00:00:23.255 --> 00:00:25.324 align:start position:0%
Yeah, we thought we'd have
a celebratory episode

00:00:25.357 --> 00:00:27.660 align:start position:0%
after being bombarded
by some online video.

00:00:27.693 --> 00:00:29.695 align:start position:0%
Something called
daytime fireworks.

00:00:29.728 --> 00:00:32.432
Just looks like giant plumes
of colored powder shooting up.

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:34.100 align:start size:56% position:44%
So, essentially
what's happened is

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:35.368 align:start size:78% position:22%
someone's seen our airbag
powder paint video

00:00:35.401 --> 00:00:37.236
<i>and thought that looks amazing.</i>

00:00:37.269 --> 00:00:38.604
<i> Let's copy it
 and make it better.</i>

00:00:38.637 --> 00:00:40.073 align:start position:0%
Yeah, that's how it happened.
They copied us.

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:42.075 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Yeah.
- Now, the video we saw

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:44.644 align:start position:0%
was at a speed that was
enjoyable by the human eye

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:46.646 align:start position:0%
but we're shooting ours
in super slow-mo.

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:48.648 align:start position:0%
So, we're gonna set ours off
much much faster.

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.450 align:start size:41% position:59%
I'll show you
what we mean.

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:53.419 align:start position:0%
Daniel, explain to us
how on Earth this works.

00:00:53.452 --> 00:00:54.821 align:start size:75% position:25%
This is a firework cake.

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:56.823 align:start size:66% position:34%
And each cake is full
of tubes.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:59.392 align:start size:75% position:25%
And each tube has one
of these little wads in.

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:02.095 align:start size:59% position:41%
And now there's
a little charge
underneath the wad.

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:04.197 align:start size:63% position:38%
On top of the wad is
our colored powder.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.432 align:start size:63% position:38%
When we initiate it,
it fires the wad up

00:01:06.465 --> 00:01:09.469 align:start size:75% position:25%
and the powder comes out
about 140 miles an hour.

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:13.172 align:start size:53% position:47%
Each one has 25
individual tubes.

00:01:13.205 --> 00:01:15.842 align:start position:0%
And we have 60 of them.

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:18.878 align:start size:78% position:22%
That's a total
of 1500 individual tubes.

00:01:18.911 --> 00:01:22.281 size:88% position:44%
And they're all gonna go off
in less than half a second.

00:01:22.314 --> 00:01:23.549 align:start size:66% position:34%
Might be kinda tricky

00:01:23.582 --> 00:01:25.318 align:start size:69% position:31%
to do it with a little
lit fuse here

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:26.819 align:start size:47% position:53%
running along
with a lighter.

00:01:26.852 --> 00:01:29.155 align:start size:78% position:22%
So we're gonna do it
electronically with these

00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:31.491 align:start size:81% position:19%
and a little sort of radio
controlled thing.

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:33.126 align:start position:0%
I think we should set up
the Phantom.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:35.161 align:start size:38% position:63%
Yep.

00:01:36.695 --> 00:01:38.264 align:start position:0%
Well, here we are.

00:01:38.297 --> 00:01:41.501 align:start position:0%
We're stood in front
of the entire 40 yard run.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:44.504 align:start position:0%
We've been told
that to propel the paint up

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:47.640 align:start position:0%
there's actually six or so feet
of just white smoke.

00:01:47.673 --> 00:01:50.176 align:start position:0%
So in order
to see the color,

00:01:50.209 --> 00:01:53.613 align:start position:0%
we've gone pretty wide
on the shot.

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.615 align:start position:0%
Look at that head room.
( laughs )

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:57.517 size:88% position:56%
Not often you need that much
head room for one of these.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:58.751 size:78% position:39%
Are you gonna try a jump?

00:01:58.784 --> 00:02:00.353 size:84% position:58%
I'm gonna do a little jump.

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:01.654 align:start size:72% position:28%
I'm not sure
how good it's gonna be.

00:02:01.687 --> 00:02:03.356 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I might be distracted, but--
- Okay.

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:05.158 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah.
- I might just do a cool pose.

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:06.425 align:start size:88% position:13%
- All right.
- Like, I can't do that.

00:02:06.458 --> 00:02:07.693 align:start position:0%
I don't know
how a cool pose looks.

00:02:07.726 --> 00:02:09.162 align:start position:0%
So I'll just--
I'll figure it out.

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:11.631 align:start size:66% position:34%
We know this already.
Are you ready?

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:13.633 align:start size:91% position:9%
- Yes.
- You got your pose ready?

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:15.501
- Yep.
- Okay.

00:02:15.534 --> 00:02:16.769 align:start size:47% position:53% line:0%
Everyone ready?

00:02:16.802 --> 00:02:18.538 line:0%
Man: Ready.

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:21.574 align:start size:69% position:31% line:0%
Three, two, one, fire.

00:02:28.747 --> 00:02:30.316
Bugger!

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:34.187 align:start size:50% position:50%
That is amazing!

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.789 align:start size:81% position:19%
I love how many explosions
there were in the air.

00:02:36.822 --> 00:02:38.558 align:start position:0%
It was like three, two, one.
I went like this...

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:39.859 align:start position:0%
Nothing happened.
I came back down,

00:02:39.892 --> 00:02:41.294 align:start position:0%
they went off
and I went...

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:42.495 align:start size:69% position:31%
I knew that
that was gonna happen.

00:02:42.528 --> 00:02:44.297 align:start size:41% position:59%
So I waited.
I was like...

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.465 align:start position:0%
- Did you feel the heat from it?
- Yeah!

00:02:46.498 --> 00:02:48.701 align:start size:81% position:19%
I was like I feel like
my legs were singed almost
but they weren't.

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:50.670 align:start size:78% position:22%
- I'm fine.
- That was mental.

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:52.405 align:start position:0%
That was wicked.

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:54.407 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Listen to that.
- Oh, that one didn't go off.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.275 align:start size:91% position:9%
- I'd stay away from that.
- Neither did these.

00:02:56.308 --> 00:02:57.743 align:start size:66% position:34%
Oh, the blues
didn't go off either.

00:02:57.776 --> 00:02:59.679 align:start size:69% position:31%
- Ugh!
- All right.

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:01.948 align:start position:0%
- Okay.
- Well I think we've got enough
for one more run.

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:04.951 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Okay.
- But first, let's have a look
at the footage.

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:08.955 align:start position:0%
Okay, so it's clear
that some didn't go off.

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:12.559 align:start position:0%
Thankfully our high speed
footage can tell us exactly
what happened there.

00:03:16.595 --> 00:03:19.565
<i>Okay, so, it was meant to start
 this end with the yellow.</i>

00:03:19.598 --> 00:03:22.268
<i> But the ones right behind me
 decided to go off.</i>

00:03:22.301 --> 00:03:25.271
<i> These are going off.</i>

00:03:25.304 --> 00:03:28.241
<i> You know that smoke is a
 lot higher than six feet.</i>

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:31.911 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Dan:<i> That's huge. </i>
- Gav:<i> We might need to adjust
 our second angle.</i>

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:35.781
Dan:<i> That looks so cool.
 Look at that.</i>

00:03:35.814 --> 00:03:37.883
Gav:<i> And we got no blue
 whatsoever.</i>

00:03:37.916 --> 00:03:39.352
<i> And blue's my favorite color.</i>

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:40.553
<i> So we have to do it again.</i>

00:03:40.586 --> 00:03:43.723
Dan:<i> Oh, no.</i>

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:46.959 align:start position:0%
All right, how about this?
Instead of just standing
in place or jumping,

00:03:46.992 --> 00:03:48.995 size:78% position:39%
why don't we just peg it?

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:50.896 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Just run.
- Absolutely leg it.

00:03:50.929 --> 00:03:52.431 align:start size:84% position:16%
Well that'll be really cool
'cause it'll show us

00:03:52.464 --> 00:03:54.000 align:start size:59% position:41%
exactly how quickly
it's going up.

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:56.369 align:start size:88% position:13%
- 'Cause we'll probably
  not be moving.
- Yeah.

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:57.637 align:start size:81% position:19%
- You ready to run?
- Yep.

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:58.971 align:start size:63% position:38%
Okay, so we're gonna
have a delay.

00:03:59.004 --> 00:04:00.640 align:start size:75% position:25%
So, it should--
we should be ahead of it

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:02.508 align:start position:0%
- and then it will overtake us.
  You ready?
- Okay.

00:04:02.541 --> 00:04:03.776 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Yeah.
- Let's do it.
  Okay, we're ready.

00:04:03.809 --> 00:04:06.012
Yeah.

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:09.249
Go!

00:04:10.716 --> 00:04:12.685
( screaming )

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:18.691
- Duck.
- Whoa!

00:04:18.724 --> 00:04:19.992
- Ooh!
- Whoa!

00:04:20.025 --> 00:04:22.295
Gav: Dan.

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:24.897 align:start position:0%
Dan: Chill out.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:27.066
- That was warm.
- That was warm.

00:04:27.099 --> 00:04:29.035
Did they all go off?
These ones didn't.

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:30.069 align:start position:0%
Oh, all these did,
though. Look.

00:04:30.102 --> 00:04:31.804
Oh, that's sweet.

00:04:31.837 --> 00:04:33.706 align:start position:0%
- You hear the sizzle.
- Yeah. Oh, that's a nice sound.

00:04:33.739 --> 00:04:35.875
Those didn't go off.

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:38.678 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's weird 'cause the fuses
must not go off
on some of them.

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:40.646 align:start size:66% position:34%
All of these went off
so it's just
the ones at the end

00:04:40.679 --> 00:04:42.682 align:start size:59% position:41%
that didn't go off.

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:47.453 align:start size:91% position:9%
- That was pretty scary.
- Let's get a look at that
footage.

00:04:47.486 --> 00:04:48.921 align:start position:0%
Where were we do you think
when it caught up?

00:04:48.954 --> 00:04:50.323 align:start size:81% position:19%
I think we were quite far,
actually.

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:52.358
I reckon I wanna say
about here.

00:04:52.391 --> 00:04:53.526
- ( laughs )
- Hang on.

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:55.428
I wanna say
like we were here.

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:58.097 align:start size:91% position:9%
- You could feel the wave
  of heat rush past.
- Yeah.

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:00.466 align:start size:97% position:3%
- It was quite nice actually.
- I think I was just screaming
the whole time.

00:05:00.499 --> 00:05:02.601 align:start size:78% position:22%
How expensive would it be
to have that

00:05:02.634 --> 00:05:05.604 align:start size:59% position:41%
as, oh, I'm feeling
a bit chilly.

00:05:05.637 --> 00:05:08.607 align:start position:0%
- Very expensive.
- Should we sell some of these?

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:10.576
Okay, let's play it.
Look at us sort of small
down there.

00:05:10.609 --> 00:05:12.645 align:start size:22% position:78%
Teensy.

00:05:12.678 --> 00:05:15.014 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Gav:<i> Booking it.
 Nicely separated. </i>
- Dan:<i> Yeah.</i>

00:05:15.047 --> 00:05:16.916
<i> I feel like a lot of the time
 when we're doing stuff
 like this,</i>

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:18.951
<i> we always cover each other up.
 So give it some--</i>

00:05:18.984 --> 00:05:21.120
<i> give it a bit of distance,
 a gap there.</i>

00:05:21.153 --> 00:05:23.356
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:29.929
<i> It went pretty quickly,
 actually.</i>

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:32.932
<i>I thought we were further ahead
 than that.</i>

00:05:37.703 --> 00:05:40.072
<i> Wow! Look at that.</i>

00:05:40.105 --> 00:05:41.941
<i> That's wicked.</i>

00:05:41.974 --> 00:05:45.111
<i> Oh, I was right,
 it was about the blue.</i>

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:47.013
Gav:<i> Oh, yeah.</i>

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:52.385
<i> I like all these little
 flayed out bits.</i>

00:05:52.418 --> 00:05:54.387
<i> Madness.</i>

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:55.621
<i> These are cool.</i>

00:05:58.157 --> 00:06:00.860
<i> What a surreal looking shot.</i>

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:03.095
<i> Look at those colors.
 That's wicked.</i>

00:06:03.128 --> 00:06:04.964
<i> It's kind of weird
 how the green color</i>

00:06:04.997 --> 00:06:06.666
<i> like they have the explosions
 still in the air.</i>

00:06:09.168 --> 00:06:11.604
<i> Instead of a big sort
 of rainbow mushroom cloud,</i>

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:13.606
<i> it looks like
 a rainbow volcano.</i>

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:16.909
Dan:<i> Yeah, with like lava
 coming out now.</i>

00:06:16.942 --> 00:06:20.079
Gav:<i> Look at that!
 The green is very sparky.</i>

00:06:20.112 --> 00:06:24.117
Dan:<i> Yeah, the green one is more
 like an evening firework.</i>

00:06:25.851 --> 00:06:27.787
Gav:<i> This wide is just
 bloody amazing.</i>

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:29.455
<i> It looks like the Muppets
 dropped a nuke.</i>

00:06:29.488 --> 00:06:31.457
<i> ( laughs )</i>

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:34.126
<i> That is the prettiest cloud
 I've ever seen.</i>

00:06:34.159 --> 00:06:36.128
Dan:<i> It looks like velvet.</i>

00:06:36.161 --> 00:06:38.164
Gav:<i> Oh, that's wonderful.</i>

00:06:40.766 --> 00:06:43.936
That was really exhilarating
to run next to.

00:06:43.969 --> 00:06:45.204 align:start size:56% position:44%
You're telling me.

00:06:45.237 --> 00:06:46.872 align:start size:66% position:34%
I was slightly closer
than you were.

00:06:46.905 --> 00:06:48.707 align:start size:81% position:19%
I was like have I got some
singed leg hairs here?

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:51.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yeah.
- No, I think I'm all right.

00:06:51.743 --> 00:06:53.579 align:start size:44% position:56%
Wouldn't wanna
be any closer.

00:06:53.612 --> 00:06:54.914
Probably not.

00:06:54.947 --> 00:06:57.550
Well, that is the smell
of success I think.

00:06:57.583 --> 00:06:58.751 align:start size:66% position:34%
Carnage, I would say.

00:06:58.784 --> 00:07:00.886 align:start position:0%
That was such
an insane moment in time.

00:07:00.919 --> 00:07:03.222 align:start size:97% position:3%
- It was wicked.
- Like when all the cloud was
  together in the air.

00:07:03.255 --> 00:07:04.824 align:start position:0%
So it only lasted
a few seconds

00:07:04.857 --> 00:07:06.559 align:start size:91% position:9%
- and then it blows away.
- It looked like--

00:07:06.592 --> 00:07:08.561 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Oh, we should probably
  put that out.
- Oh, goodness.

00:07:08.594 --> 00:07:10.663 align:start size:69% position:31%
This is fully on fire.

00:07:10.696 --> 00:07:12.198 align:start size:91% position:9%
- Give it a little squirt.
- Oh!

00:07:12.231 --> 00:07:14.066 align:start size:59% position:41%
I think we're good.

00:07:14.099 --> 00:07:16.836 align:start position:0%
Well, I thought that was
a lovely fitting end
to "Planet Slow Mo."

00:07:16.869 --> 00:07:19.205 align:start position:0%
We ended up back in Texas
where we started.

00:07:19.238 --> 00:07:20.739 size:84% position:42%
That was insanely colorful.

00:07:20.772 --> 00:07:22.107
Hopefully you enjoyed
the series.

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:24.143
Feel free to subscribe
to the Slow Mo guys

00:07:24.176 --> 00:07:26.512
and check out all
the previous episodes.

00:07:26.545 --> 00:07:28.013
What we made.

00:07:28.046 --> 00:07:30.950
Should we go and clear up
that massive mess?

00:07:30.983 --> 00:07:33.619
- Yeah, all right,
  probably should.
- I'll get a rake.

